    "fullTextHtml": "",
    "fullTextTemplate": "",
    "lawCode": "",
    "lawSection": "Rockland County",
    "memo": "BILL NUMBER:S4266\n\nTITLE OF BILL:\n\nAn act relating to the transfer and conveyance of certain lands to\nJoseph's Home, Inc.\n\nPURPOSE OR GENERAL IDEA OF BILL:\n\nThe purpose of this bill is to assist Joseph's Home, Inc. to expand\nthe services it provides by authorizing a transfer of portion of the\nRockland Psychiatric Center to Joseph's Home, Inc.\n\nSUMMARY OF SPECIFIC PROVISIONS:\n\nThis bill authorizes the commissioner of general services, upon the\nconsent of the commissioner of mental health, to transfer and convey\nfor one dollar a 1.461 acre parcel of unused state land located at the\nRockland Psychiatric Center to Joseph's Home, Inc.\n\nJoseph's Home Inc. is required to submit an application for transfer\nand an accurate survey of the parcel to the commissioner of general\nservices within one year of the effective date of this act.\n\nThe lands transferred to Joseph's Home, Inc. would only be able to be\nused for supportive and transitional housing for homeless and disabled\nindividuals, and other community services to prevent homelessness. If\nthe lands should ever cease to be used for these purposes, title to\nthe lands would revert back to the state of New York.\n\nJUSTIFICATION:\n\nJoseph's Home, Inc. will be able to use this parcel land at the\nRockland Psychiatric Center that is not being used by the state in\norder to expand the scope of services they offer to homeless and\ndisabled individuals. This land transfer will benefit both the\nindividuals served by Joseph's Home, Inc. as well as the state.\n\nPRIOR LEGISLATIVE HISTORY:\n\nNew bill.\n\nFISCAL IMPLICATIONS FOR STATE AND LOCAL GOVERNMENTS:\n\nNone.\n\nEFFECTIVE DATE:\n\nImmediately.\n\n",
