    "lawSection": "Rockland County",
    "memo": "BILL NUMBER:S4266A\n\nTITLE OF BILL:\n\nAn act relating to the transfer and conveyance of certain lands to\nJoseph's Home, Inc.\n\nPURPOSE OR GENERAL IDEA OF BILL:\n\nThe purpose of this bill is to assist Joseph's Home, Inc. to expand the\nservices it provides by authorizing a transfer of portion of the Rock-\nland Psychiatric Center to Joseph's Home, Inc in consideration of fair\nmarket value.\n\nSUMMARY OF SPECIFIC PROVISIONS:\n\nThis bill authorizes the commissioner of general services, upon the\nconsent of the commissioner of mental health, to transfer and convey for\none dollar a 1.461 acre parcel of unused state land located at the Rock-\nland Psychiatric Center to Joseph's Home, Inc.\n\nJoseph's Home Inc. is required to submit an application for transfer and\nan accurate survey of the parcel to the commissioner of general services\nwithin one year of the effective date of this act.\n\nThe lands transferred to Joseph's Home, Inc. would only be able to be\nused for supportive and transitional housing for homeless and disabled\nindividuals, and other community services to prevent homelessness.\n\nJUSTIFICATION:\n\nJoseph's Home, Inc. will be able to use this parcel land at the Rockland\nPsychiatric Center that is not being used by the state in order to\nexpand the scope of services they offer to homeless and disabled indi-\nviduals. This land transfer will benefit both the individuals served by\nJoseph's Home, Inc. as well as the state.\n\nPRIOR LEGISLATIVE HISTORY:\n\nNew bill.\n\nFISCAL IMPLICATIONS FOR STATE AND LOCAL GOVERNMENTS:\n\nNone.\n\nEFFECTIVE DATE:\n\nImmediately.\n\n",
